meta {
  name: 08 Error — missing targets (400)
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/factgraph/{{ruleset_id}}/query
  body: json
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
}

body:json {
  {}
}

docs {
  POST a query with no `targets`. The API responds with HTTP 400 and an
  RFC 9457 Problem Details body:

      {
        "type":   "https://tools.ietf.org/html/rfc9457",
        "title":  "Invalid targets",
        "status": 400,
        "detail": "Request body must include a non-empty \"targets\" array..."
      }

  All error responses in this API follow the same shape (`type`, `title`,
  `status`, `detail`). Clients can render `detail` directly to the user
  or branch on `status`/`title` for typed handling.

  Also fails the same way: targets that's not an array, an empty array,
  or an array containing non-string / empty-string entries.
}
